# The trial of pod-hold in podnet: the generic core of the hold of
# podnet-netns moves to pod-hold (PodUtils/podnet#414 and #422).
# seccomp/filter.rs, seccomp/notif.rs, seccomp/mem.rs, fdtable.rs,
# netns/fdpass.rs and the setup of netns/tun.rs become glue over pod-hold
# with podnet's names; seccomp/mod.rs starts the program with
# pod_hold::spawn and takes each notification with pod_hold::listen;
# netns/mod.rs enters the namespace and maps the ids with pod_hold::netns.
# The handlers, the rules, the upstreams, the relays, doctor and the CLI
# stay. src/warp/tun.rs takes TUNSETIFF of pod-hold (the number of the
# target). The test the_filter_covers_the_bypass_surfaces and the four tests of
# fdtable.rs move to pod-hold. Each podcrates tag moves to the tag of the
# hand-off. The record, the size and the layers of the files, the build,
# the bans and the sources of cargo-deny, clippy, the tests of podnet-netns,
# the integration tests of the pod (seccomp and netns), doctor, docs and the
# API, no ioctl number of the core left in podnet, the fuzz targets with
# their lock, rustfmt, each Rust toolchain of the workflows and build images
# against the rust-version of podcrates, and the binary for x86_64 musl,
# built with zig (a debug build: the release profile takes LTO), with
# podnet's static check of it.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
python3 scripts/check-layers.py
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
cargo tree -q -p podnet-netns -i pod-hold > /dev/null
! git grep -n -i -E "^[^/]*(0x4018_2103|0xc050_2100|0x4004_54ca|0x4008_2102)" -- crates src
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podnet -p podnet-netns -p podnet-core -- -D warnings
cargo test -q -p podnet-netns
cargo test -q -p podnet --test pod_seccomp_tcp --test pod_seccomp_dgram --test pod_seccomp_fds --test pod_seccomp_handoff --test pod_seccomp_nonblock --test pod_seccomp_rules --test pod_seccomp_slow_dial --test pod_seccomp_diff --test pod_backend_line --test pod_usage --test af_inet_kernel --test doctor --test docs --test api_surface
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podnet --bin podnet
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podnet"
